        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check B in both triangles",
      "body": "<p>Use the angle sum to calculate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math> for each choice of the opposite angle. Require <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math> to be positive and less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>90</mn><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup></mrow></math> in both triangles.</p>",
      "recap": "All three angles of a nondegenerate triangle are positive and add to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>180</mn><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup></mrow></math>.",
      "pitfall": "Check the acute-angle condition twice, not just in one triangle.",
